                    title: "Given a customer scenario, decide when to use virtualized data and describe virtualized data options",
                    topics: [
                        StudyTopic(id: "s18_given_a_customer_scenario_decide_when_to_1", number: 1, question: "What is Salesforce Connect and how do external objects differ from custom objects in terms of data residency, query behavior, and storage consumption?", answer: "Salesforce Connect is a framework that creates external objects—Salesforce objects that proxy data from an external system in real time via an adapter (OData, Cross-Org, Custom Apex). Data residency: data lives in the external system; Salesforce stores only the object schema definition, not the records. Query behavior: SOQL queries on external objects are translated into OData or API calls to the external system; results are returned dynamically. This means query performance depends on the external system's response time. Storage: zero Salesforce data storage consumed for record data (only the schema definition is stored). Custom objects store data in Salesforce's database—subject to storage limits but enabling full SOQL, triggers, automation, and reporting. External objects enable real-time data virtualization without replication cost.")
                    ]
                )
            ]
        )

